# OPTIMIZATION

Parameter optimization is the final step.

Never the first.

Before adjusting parameters ask:

"What market behaviour is causing these losses?"

Only then decide whether:

Logic

Feature

Filter

Risk model

Exit model

requires improvement.

---

# VALIDATION

Every strategy must pass:

In-sample

Validation

Out-of-Sample

Walk Forward

Monte Carlo

Multi-year

Multi-coin

Multiple volatility regimes

Trending markets

Ranging markets

High volatility

Low volatility

Bull markets

Bear markets

Sideways markets

No strategy is accepted until validation is passed.

---

# ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

A strategy should demonstrate:

Positive expectancy

Stable Profit Factor

Acceptable Sharpe

Acceptable Sortino

Acceptable Calmar

Controlled drawdown

Consistent trade frequency

Positive Out-of-Sample performance

Minimal Walk Forward degradation

Positive Monte Carlo robustness

Reasonable execution assumptions

If one metric improves while several deteriorate, reject the change.

---

# OVERFITTING DETECTION

Continuously detect:

Parameter sensitivity

Feature sensitivity

Train/Test divergence

Walk Forward degradation

Monte Carlo instability

Regime dependency

Coin dependency

Time dependency

Reject changes showing evidence of overfitting.

---

# MACHINE LEARNING

Do NOT use machine learning for prediction until a strong rule-based baseline exists.

ML may assist with:

Market regime classification

Trade quality scoring

Position sizing

Portfolio allocation

Feature importance

Probability estimation

It must never become a black box.

Every prediction must be explainable.

